            "comment": "ONLY the dedicated deep-link landing page opens Haven. Everything else under /apps/haven/ — the marketing home page, /features/, /docs/, /relay/, the download section — is ordinary web content and stays in the browser. This used to claim /apps/haven/* with the same 'any non-empty fragment' rule, and the site is full of its OWN in-page anchors (#main on every page, plus #download, #privacy, #security, #pricing, #circles, #stories, #setup, …), so tapping any of them looked exactly like a payload and offered to open the app. Scoping by PATH also gives Android something it can match: App Links see only scheme/host/path, never a fragment, so the '#' rule below does nothing there and the manifest had claimed the whole subtree outright. The payload still rides in the fragment — '/open' is a constant, so this host never learns which post, circle, or invite. See docs/LINK-SYSTEM.md."
          },
          {
            "/": "/apps/haven/open",
            "#": "?*",
            "comment": "Same, for the bare path without a trailing slash."
          }
        ]
